course: dictionary
lesson: 4366
title: Gust: a sudden rush of wind
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A gust is a sudden, strong rush of wind. It comes and goes quickly, unlike a steady breeze. «A sudden cool gust of wind often comes just before a thunderstorm arrives.» The words sudden and cool tell you the wind arrives all at once.
explain: Stories use gusts to start the action. If a gust blows a hat away or slams a door, the words around it give you the clue. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A sudden strong rush of wind fits, so that is the meaning.
explain: Gust can also be a verb. «The wind began to gust across the beach» means the wind blew in sudden strong bursts. A gust can also be a sudden burst of rain, smoke or laughter, so look at the words near it to find which one the author means.
fact: A gust is a sudden strong rush of wind.
fact: «Gust» can also mean a sudden burst of something, like rain, smoke or laughter.
fact: As a verb, «gust» means that wind blows in sudden strong bursts, as in «gusting wind».
fact: Strong gusts can knock things over, bend trees and make cycling dangerous.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «A sudden cool gust of wind often comes just before a thunderstorm arrives.» What is a gust? | A slow, gentle breeze on a sunny day | A roll of thunder | *A sudden strong rush of wind | A kind of cloud
exercise: Rain came in a gust against the window. What does gust mean here? | A dry, sunny day | A puddle on the path | A slow drip down the glass | *A sudden burst of rain
exercise: «The wind began to gust across the beach.» What does gust mean here? | To shine brightly | To sleep quietly | *To blow in sudden strong bursts | To walk slowly
test: Why is a strong gust dangerous when you ride a bike near traffic? | It makes your bike shine brighter | It stops the wheels from turning | *It can push you into the road | It makes the road dry
test: «The children burst out in a gust of laughter.» What does this tell you? | They were cold and wet | They sat very quietly | They ran away from the park | *They laughed suddenly, all at once
exam: In «gusting wind», what does gusting mean? | Staying perfectly still all day | Made of water and falling down | *Blowing in sudden strong bursts | Feeling warm and calm
